course: dictionary
lesson: 7579
title: Pretending and what it means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pretending means acting as if something is true when it is not. Often it is part of a game, like «Games are for the screen; the fun bit off-screen is the pretending.» Here the pretending is the make-believe fun away from the screen.
explain: Pretending can also mean trying to trick people by acting falsely. Pretending to be ill just to skip school is not a game. The same word can mean fun or trickery, so look at the clues around it.
explain: «Everyone acts a bit differently in different places; your real self includes all of these, though constant pretending can feel tiring.» The clue tiring tells you that pretending here means acting a part all the time, and that it can wear you out.
explain: Pretending is a verb (pretend, pretends, pretended, pretending), and pretending can also be a noun for the act itself. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence: does acting as if it is true still make sense?
fact: Pretending means acting as if something is true when it is not.
fact: Pretend play, make-believe and role play are all forms of pretending.
fact: Phrases to know: pretending to, pretending that, and stop pretending.
fact: Some people online pretend to be someone else, for example a child, so never share personal details with them.
fact: If you are pretending to be fine when you are not, it is OK to tell a trusted adult.
exercise: Ruby is pretending to be a dragon in the playground. What is she doing? | Lost in the woods | Telling the truth about her homework | *Acting as if she is a dragon, in a game | Sleeping under the slide
exercise: «Games are for the screen; the fun bit off-screen is the pretending.» What is the pretending in this sentence? | The rules of the game | The screen itself | *The make-believe fun away from the screen | A broken toy
exercise: Which sentence shows pretending as tricking people? | Ella is pretending to be a princess in drama | *Sam pretends to be ill so he does not have to go to school | Maya pretends to be a pirate at break time | Leo is pretending his teddy is a baby in his game
test: Some people online pretend to be a child. What should you do? | Tell them your address so they can be your friend | *Never share personal details with them | Send them a photo of your house | Give them your password
test: «Constant pretending can feel tiring.» What does pretending mean in this sentence? | Sleeping late at the weekend | *Acting a part all the time, which can wear you out | Singing loudly in class | Winning a race
exam: Maya keeps pretending to be fine when she is really sad. What is a good thing for her to do? | Pretend harder so nobody notices | Pretend to be ill to skip school | *Tell a trusted adult that she is not fine | Hide in her room forever
